########################### METHODS ###########################
1. text()
-> Selects element based on their text.
//tagname[text()='textvalue']
-> example:
//option[text()="Python"]

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. contains()
-> selects element based on partial value or partial text
-> we can use any portion of the sentence/value. Not just first
//tagname[contains(@attribute,'substring')] or //tagname[contains(text(),'substring')]
->example:
//option[contains(text(),"Play")]

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. starts-with():
-> elements whose attribute value or text content starts with a specific substring.
-> //tagname[starts-with(@attribute,'substring')] or //tagname[starts-with(text(),'substring')]
->example:
//button[starts-with(text(),'Normal')]
//button[starts-with(@type,'res')]

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. and/or operator:
-> combine multiple conditions in an XPath expression.
-> //tagname[@attribute1='value1' and @attribute2='value2'] or 
//tagname[@attribute1='value1' or @attribute2='value2']
-> example:
//input[@id='disabledInput' or @value='Disabled']
/input[@type='text' and @value='Enabled']